WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.227
An extraordinary car deserves an experience to match. This independent LavishCars concept brings a

00:00:07.227 --> 00:00:13.473
considered marketplace, clear rental rates, and direct supplier inquiries into one journey. Start

00:00:13.473 --> 00:00:19.719
with the product: a premium storefront designed for discovery, with dedicated workspaces for

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:21.160
suppliers and administrators.

00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:28.583
Explore by destination, brand, model, category and budget. Refine by passengers, transmission and

00:00:28.583 --> 00:00:34.807
features, then compare daily, weekly or monthly prices. Vehicle details bring photos, specifications

00:00:34.807 --> 00:00:41.509
and related offers together. A structured quote request records the customer’s interest against the

00:00:41.509 --> 00:00:48.211
correct supplier and vehicle. This is an inquiry marketplace; payment and confirmed reservations are

00:00:48.211 --> 00:00:49.647
outside the prototype.

00:00:50.847 --> 00:00:56.887
The supplier dashboard keeps the operation in view: listing states, fleet management and incoming

00:00:56.887 --> 00:01:02.927
inquiries. Suppliers can create an offer, edit specifications and rental periods, order photos, and

00:01:02.927 --> 00:01:08.967
submit it for review. Profile, team membership and service areas have dedicated controls. Private

00:01:08.967 --> 00:01:15.007
records stay scoped to the authenticated supplier, while pause and archive actions support the

00:01:15.007 --> 00:01:15.869
listing lifecycle.

00:01:17.069 --> 00:01:21.687
The administrator workspace controls supplier approval, listing moderation and publication.

00:01:21.687 --> 00:01:29.075
Reviewers can approve, reject with a reason, hide an offer or suspend a supplier. Catalog and

00:01:29.075 --> 00:01:35.078
location controls cover brands, models, categories and the market hierarchy. These actions are

00:01:35.078 --> 00:01:41.081
enforced in the backend. An ineligible offer disappears from public discovery and recommendations,

00:01:41.081 --> 00:01:43.852
while its business history remains available.

00:01:45.052 --> 00:01:52.452
Here is the complete business flow, verified through the API. A new supplier offer is private before

00:01:52.452 --> 00:01:58.547
approval. Once approved, the same offer becomes publicly accessible. A fictional customer request is

00:01:58.547 --> 00:02:04.642
saved, and the responsible supplier can retrieve it in their inbox. Inquiry and notification-outbox

00:02:04.642 --> 00:02:10.301
records commit together. The local WordPress bridge also displays eligible inventory, preserving a

00:02:10.301 --> 00:02:12.477
path toward the existing website.

00:02:13.677 --> 00:02:21.429
Now, the intelligence. A visitor asks for a luxury SUV in Dubai, for four days, below one thousand

00:02:21.429 --> 00:02:27.457
dirhams a day. The concierge interprets supported constraints and returns up to three eligible

00:02:27.457 --> 00:02:33.917
database offers. In this verified response: a Cadillac Escalade at eight hundred fifty, a Range

00:02:33.917 --> 00:02:42.099
Rover Sport at nine hundred, and a G Class at nine hundred ninety dirhams per day. Prices, seats and

00:02:42.099 --> 00:02:47.697
explanations come from the catalog. Missing destinations can trigger a clarification without losing

00:02:47.697 --> 00:02:48.558
earlier preferences.

00:02:49.758 --> 00:02:55.850
Preference recommendations keep mandatory constraints intact, with transparent category and occasion

00:02:55.850 --> 00:03:03.603
weights. Suppliers get a second practical assistant: rough notes become suggested vehicle fields, a

00:03:03.603 --> 00:03:10.249
description and completeness warnings. Preview, apply, edit, save and submit remain distinct

00:03:10.249 --> 00:03:16.894
actions. Suggestions never publish a car automatically. The no-key demonstration uses deterministic

00:03:16.894 --> 00:03:24.093
interpretation; an optional external-model adapter is implemented, but a live provider call remains

00:03:24.093 --> 00:03:24.647
unverified.

00:03:25.847 --> 00:03:31.402
The remaining assistance supports daily operations. Scoped insights summarize recorded listings,

00:03:31.402 --> 00:03:36.451
inquiries, category interest and detail-page activity. Photo assistance checks resolution,

00:03:36.451 --> 00:03:43.015
brightness and edge detail, flags normalized duplicate uploads, and suggests cover candidates. These

00:03:43.015 --> 00:03:49.074
are descriptive summaries and image-quality heuristics. View counts include repeated API requests,

00:03:49.074 --> 00:03:54.123
and photo checks do not verify vehicle identity or ownership.

00:03:55.323 --> 00:04:03.451
Behind the experience are Next J S, Fast API and PostgreSQL, with a separate WordPress bridge. Local

00:04:03.451 --> 00:04:08.710
verification includes twenty-two backend tests, four main browser scenarios, seven additional

00:04:08.710 --> 00:04:16.360
interface checks and five proxy checks. The public review page brings the film, source code and

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:22.097
technical roadmap together. Prepared by Ayman Lakhnati after the technical assessment: an

00:04:22.097 --> 00:04:27.356
independent concept, developed with AI assistance. Synthetic inventory, edited prototype captures,

00:04:27.356 --> 00:04:34.527
and neural voice narration. I would welcome the opportunity to discuss the decisions behind it.
